{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure","id":774526,"title":"Question about the Pure","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-11-25T21:22:22-08:00","id":774526,"title":"Question about the Pure","content":"One thing that always confused me about the Pure is why would Luna punish them if their founders had nothing to do with Father Wolf's death? Anyone knows? Am I missing something obvious? Did Luna mess up or is she just a bitch?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:34:52-08:00","id":774535,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure#post774526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that always confused me about the Pure is why would Luna punish them if their founders had nothing to do with Father Wolf's death?</div> </div> </div> </div>The world rotted and they did nothing. Their siblings plotted patricide and they did nothing. He died and they did nothing.<br /> <br /> He was their father. Their having nothing to do with his death is part of the problem and rewarding them for letting it happen is the opposite of how a boundary god is likely to respond to inattentiveness.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Did Luna mess up or is she just a bitch? </div> </div> </div>Neither. Being the nearest named entity in the Shadow to Fate itself in practical terms means you tend to have a pretty competent grasp of what you need to accomplish your goals, and the Queen of the Night is neither in the habit of telling what those are nor able to speak for herself directly by dint of her being the goddamn Moon.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T21:52:16-08:00","id":774543,"title":"","content":"A moon who is supposedly the lover of a wolf that is also sapient enough to acknowledge when her dog is put down and curse the off-spring as well to avenge him; forgive me if I don't use rationality when addressing supernatural origin myths. That said, as unfair and unjustified as I feel it is; it does answer my question. I can imagine they get more cursed when they start giving the finger instead of getting to work like the Forsaken which explains their current state; thanks for the clarification.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T22:03:08-08:00","id":774548,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure?p=774543#post774543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A moon who is supposedly the lover of a wolf that is also sapient enough to acknowledge when her dog is put down and curse the off-spring as well to avenge him; forgive me if I don't use rationality when addressing supernatural origin myths.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure why you'd think I was making a statement of sapience rather than scale when talking about a spirit.<br /> <br /> Luna is The Moon. There's not a lot of widely-acknowledged animistic beings that fall under the same umbrella as her re: &quot;too big to actually manifest.&quot;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-25T23:53:25-08:00","id":774572,"title":"","content":"Well when I hear &quot;Moon&quot; I think &quot;Big rock in space&quot; which Luna is presumably more than given the things she do (at least in myth), so I read &quot;she's the goddamn moon&quot; I basically read &quot;it's just a rock in space&quot; which might've been a misunderstanding on my part. That said tho, if she's half as powerful as the myths say I'd presume she's capable of speaking without having to manifest in full-scale or any such. Whether she'd actually care to is another thing of course but that's neither here nor there as far as I'm concerned given the topic being on the Pure's punishment first and foremost. I feel it's cleared up that she did it because of their passiveness at best and laziness at worst and whether it was just or not well, even if it wasn't it's not like it could keep it from happening; especially not in the World of Darkness of all places. So for me, the pieces are in place.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7060-karavolos","name":"Karavolos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7060_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"163"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T00:44:41-08:00","id":774590,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure?p=774572#post774572\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well when I hear &quot;Moon&quot; I think &quot;Big rock in space&quot; which Luna is presumably more than given the things she do (at least in myth), so I read &quot;she's the goddamn moon&quot; I basically read &quot;it's just a rock in space&quot; which might've been a misunderstanding on my part. That said tho, if she's half as powerful as the myths say I'd presume she's capable of speaking without having to manifest in full-scale or any such. Whether she'd actually care to is another thing of course but that's neither here nor there as far as I'm concerned given the topic being on the Pure's punishment first and foremost. I feel it's cleared up that she did it because of their passiveness at best and laziness at worst and whether it was just or not well, even if it wasn't it's not like it could keep it from happening; especially not in the World of Darkness of all places. So for me, the pieces are in place.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think Cahaliths get those fancy dreams?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":576,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","user":"Ephsy","date":". 11-26-2015, 09:16 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:09:54-08:00","id":774604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure#post774526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that always confused me about the Pure is why would Luna punish them if their founders had nothing to do with Father Wolf's death? Anyone knows? Am I missing something obvious? Did Luna mess up or is she just a bitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha are forsaken by Iduth.<br /> Iduth is forsaken by Anshega.<br /> That's the trick. Luna blessed her fallen children because they wanted to restore balance, or by the way, <i>do something </i>about the consequences of the death of Urfarah.<br /> Because they accepted the fact that his death messed up a lot of things, they accepted their duty.<br /> But the Pure, well, we have to understand their hate culture. It's not very simple I guess. Iduth is of course mad (at least for almost every ''this story is true''), but for the pure she's also a total bitch. She accepted the murderer of father wolf blessing them with auspicies and powerful gifts, even if in the first time she cursed them with silver. The pure are just cursed.<br /> The pure ancestors were all about hunt, kill, eat, fuck, instinct, worship Urfarah after glorious hunt.<br /> Also, in the first edition you can find a lot of ''this story is true'' about their fristbron threatened by Luna in a way or another.<br /> When the worlds collapses the pure just don't understand such a humiliation. After all, they were more human in this than the forsaken: the forsaken accepted the natural order, killing their weak father, the strong prevail. The pure didn't accept this vision, for them it was a murder. Pure deicide.<br /> The real reason about the pure culture lies after the death of father wolf: the forsaken are blessed by Luna after they swear an oath to the firstborn to accept theyr sacred duties after father wolf's death, for the pure this is pure madness, they consdier themselves pure because <b><i>they just didn't kill their father</i></b>.<br /> And after all, werewolves just not ''believe'' in spirits and the moon: they can live and see their faith. They have real evidence about spirits, Lunes, Moon, Father Wolf.<br /> Their religion is true, is alive, it's not like christianity or islam where you have to have faith.<br /> In reality, for example, christianity and islam have had scions and idealists, we have a lot of type of faith, catholic, ortodox, protestant, shia islam, sunni islam: imagine that for werewolves, BUT they also see and lives the reality of religion.<br /> Also, like for political and religious party, werewolves follow some kind of ''symbol'' and ''leader'', the firstborn.<br /> And, let's say, the pure firstborn aren't exactly the portrait of sanity.<br /> And they also has social relationship with the other firstborn: Uzuruth ur and Fenris ur hate themselves, Hathis ur is obsessed with purity, he jus't can't accept to become the totem of a degenerate-murder child, and also he keeps grudge against Skolis ur, Gurim is the last of the firstborn, some kind of mad god who finds wisdom through his madness, always protected by Hathis from what I remember. All, Uzuruth, Hathis and Gurim, has something different from the other firstborn: in a way or another, they are extreme, talking about concept. Follow one of them require to unleash an ancient hate and istinct, to kill your human side and live as the best predator on the earth, so yes, from ancient eras, they forged a total hate culture made of grudge and revenge.<br /> In the first edition Pure core book you can find a lot of explanation and information about their brainwashing culture.<br /> But this kind of themes are current even in human world, sadly <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> Last but not less important, I think they are ''romantic'' artistically talking. You can use the pure showing some kind of forgotten human nature, they took what they want, they fight, hunt, kills, love, hate, in an extreme way, you can try to see them also like some kind of nature-twisted revenge against human concept.<br /> <br /> <br /> Of course, this is how I explain to myself the Pure. Hope you find it useful. The pure are one of the best antagonist to my point of view, they reflect a lot of current themes about human and religious nature.<br /> Sorry for my rusty english.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":3773,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","user":"Helur","date":". 11-26-2015, 04:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T01:24:32-08:00","id":774613,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure#post774526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that always confused me about the Pure is why would Luna punish them if their founders had nothing to do with Father Wolf's death?</div> </div> </div> </div>Why do you think Luna did not interfere? For example in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/137256-alternative-werewolves-myths#post137256\">Scandinavian version of Pangae myth</a> it's Father Moon that talked Forsaken in to killing Mother of Wolves. There are literal hundreds version of this tale - I assume in some it's Father Luna that could talked Forsaken in to murder.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure#post774526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Did Luna mess up or is she just a bitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>She/He is god/dess of Shadow, beside the Moon, more immersed in politics of spirits and Lunes than her own descendents. Comes from <b>outside of this planet</b>, like Ivory Claws point it out. He change this moods as his faces. She is fickle and whimsical. And even do not show on day to day basis to her (grand)children, most do not see she/he any time in his Uratha lives. What <i>parent</i> it it?<br /> <br /> And is known to <b>dictate your entire Uratha life</b> by First Changing you under the Auspice he/she thinks is good. Think of it - you are soldier in your pre-Change life. You are prepared to kill humans, prepare tactics and is enjoying battle. But then comes Change, and you must be puny Shaman of Crescent Moon than glorious Warrior of Full Moon? <b><i>Hell NO!!!</i></b> ( I think it's one of main reasons Pure survive all the time - there always will be Uratha do not agreeing with their Auspice chosen under First Change. )<br /> <br /> Thinking on all of this, I can easily see Luna as <i>really</i> bad parent to her family. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/redface.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Embarrassment\" smilieid=\"2\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 11-26-2015, 04:34 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T02:27:42-08:00","id":774628,"title":"","content":"The Uratha's myths regarding their origin and the death of father wolf are just that - myths. They're not supposed to be 100% true in-universe. See a contradiction? That probably means somewhere along the line something got twisted. Maybe the <i>Pure</i> helped kill father wolf, and over time they rationalised it and started blaming the forsaken for suckering them in and eventually the new generations have forgotten what happened and believe their own lies about not being responsible. <br /> <br /> So maybe Luna is punishing them for something they not only did, but refuse to apologise for and refuse to try to rectify the problems it caused. <br /> <br /> Plot hooks!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T03:48:11-08:00","id":774649,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Karavolos</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/774526-question-about-the-pure#post774526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One thing that always confused me about the Pure is why would Luna punish them if their founders had nothing to do with Father Wolf's death? Anyone knows? Am I missing something obvious? Did Luna mess up or is she just a bitch?</div> </div> </div> </div>I still like the interpretation where Luna punished all werewolves for the death of Father Wolf, no matter who was responsible. It was only when five of the tribes sought the forgiveness of Luna that their curse was lessened. According to this interpretation the difference between the Pure and the Forsaken is not that Luna inflicted a stronger curse upon the Pure, but that the Pure refused to ask her for forgiveness.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T04:03:36-08:00","id":774661,"title":"","content":"Basically, you need to remember that the Pure are probably full of shit. I mean, they deride the Forsaken for being Luna's slaves when they're basically their totem's low-level grunts. They can't see the wood for the trees.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T04:14:30-08:00","id":774668,"title":"","content":"I think it's fair to say the modern Pure are very much hypocritical zealots fighting for a lost homeland they never knew, wanting power without responsibility and privilege without duty.<br /> <br /> The 'original' Pure far less so, but how much they should be blamed for inaction before even considering mythological inaccuracies is debatable. As is that they (and the rest of the Uratha) deserved Luna's punishment at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":188,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","user":"YeOfLittleFaith","date":". 11-26-2015, 07:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-11-26T05:56:03-08:00","id":774710,"title":"","content":"this could help you to understand the pure, and maybe why they are cursed wrost than the forsaken by Iduth:<br /> <br /> <i>This story\u2019s true.<br /> You\u2019ve been lied to, boy. All the important parts were<br /> sold to you as an honest tale, but in your heart I think you<br /> see what\u2019s right. Your blood stirs to old memories that haven\u2019t<br /> been told to you, not yet. Time to change that, I figure.<br /> We were the kings of the country, once upon a time.<br /> Pangaea was our territory, the forest in which we hunted. We<br /> sat at the very top of that food chain \u2014 all the beasts of the<br /> wood and spirits in the Shadow bent knee to us and our alpha,<br /> Father Wolf. None dared disrupt the balance that we had so<br /> carefully forged. The human apes scurried back to their trees<br /> at the sight of us. Birds flew from our snapping jaws. Even<br /> the tangled vines and bright flowers recoiled from us for fear<br /> of earning our ire. All was good. Father Wolf \u2014 Urfarah<br /> \u2014 was a proper father, caring for his children and raising us<br /> right.<br /> But she figured out how to make it all fall down. That<br /> bitch \u2014 our Mother \u2014 helped betray Father and tear the<br /> worlds asunder. <b>Those others, they\u2019d tell you that Luna was<br /> powerful and joyous, and that she truly loved Father when<br /> she came down and offered herself to him. It wasn\u2019t like that.<br /> The manipulative creature, that thing with moods and faces<br /> as fickle as those she shows in the sky above \u2014 she was lonely<br /> and useless sitting way up there in the dark sky. She wanted a<br /> piece of what Father had: dominion, authority, power. Mother<br /> Moon knew she couldn\u2019t just take it from him, for he would\u2019ve<br /> bitten her clean in twain would she have tried.</b> So, she needed<br /> to take it from him piece by piece, sucking it from him like a<br /> patient leech.<br /> We helped do him in, but not in the way that the others</i><br /> did. When she gave birth to us and he raised us in his image,<br /> it was a distraction. Our nativity drained him. Our training<br /> and raising sapped his strength. And all the while, behind the<br /> scenes, she made sure that the spirits found him during times<br /> of weakness. Luna set upon him with her own magic, the<br /> same magic that spooks the human herd when they see us in<br /> our true and rightful forms. Madness crept in at the edges of<br /> Urfarah, and we were blind to it.<br /> At least, we were up to the point when it was too late.<br /> All the while, Mother Moon grew in power and Father Wolf<br /> was losing his, and we sat idly by, performing our duties and<br /> ignoring what was obvious.<br /> <b>When Luna came to us with the suggestion, that\u2019s when<br /> it became clear as crystal waters. Shit, it was her idea, that<br /> Father\u2019s children take his place. She came to the nine tribes<br /> of those nine pups and pleaded with us to do what was right,<br /> to make real what had to be done. Some of the others \u2014 too<br /> many of the others \u2014 agreed</b>. They had suckled long at her<br /> sweet teat, trusting her pretty white face and believing that<br /> one\u2019s mother must always have the best intentions at heart.<br /> <b>Those kinslayers did what we would not. They brought down<br /> Urfarah. Tore out his throat, and the blood that spilled was<br /> the last pure blood that washed the land.<br /> But we didn\u2019t take part. We tried to stop the betrayers,<br /> led by their noses, but there wasn\u2019t enough of us to save him.<br /> Now, we\u2019re the last keepers of that pure blood. We stood in<br /> it as Father\u2019s body cooled, the blood growing thick and sticky<br /> around our feet, and we all drank of it.</b> Now, some of that<br /> blood churns through our veins still, running hot with acid and<br /> anger.<br /> Father Wolf was betrayed by Mother Moon. Isn\u2019t any<br /> other way to see it. And now, those who wear the brands that<br /> glow with her tainted touch, they think they have themselves<br /> badges of honor. They\u2019re wrong. They have slave collars.<br /> Marks of shame. Bitter burns of treachery. They are truly<br /> Forsaken, those animals. The Shadow turns away from the<br /> degenerates, but it doesn\u2019t turn from us. We shed ourselves<br /> of the bitch\u2019s brand, and by doing so the spirits know that we<br /> have cut out the human cancer.<br /> We let the Forsaken destroy the greatest thing we\u2019d ever<br /> had because we were deaf, dumb and blind. Worse, there<br /> weren\u2019t enough of us. That\u2019s why our numbers have grown.<br /> That\u2019s why we outnumber the degenerates. Because it\u2019s time<br /> to remake the world in Urfarah\u2019s image.<br /> We are the Pure, and may Mother\u2019s children tremble and<br /> wail with our approach","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#800000\">-'' </span>We are the unsullied.<br /> We are the inheritors.<br /> We are the Pure <span style=\"color:#800000\">''-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3773-helur","name":"Helur","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3773_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"352"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}